From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poyu Chen <me@poyu.xyz>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: twl6030-irq: make the TWL6030 interrupt a working wake
 source

Two problems kept a TWL6030 child (power button, RTC alarm) from waking
the system, seen on the Zebra WT41N0:

- The child irq_chip is a copy of dummy_irq_chip, which has
  IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE: the core never calls twl6030_irq_set_wake(), the
  wake requests are not counted, and the PM notifier never arms the
  TWL6030 interrupt. Clear the flag.

- The PM notifier disables the interrupt for the suspend. The line is
  level-triggered: an interrupt arriving while it is disabled (the GPADC
  raises them regularly) masks it until resume. Keep it enabled when it is
  a wake source; once the core suspends the interrupts, an armed line
  wakes the system without running its handler, so the suspended I2C bus
  is not touched. Disable it as before when nothing needs it.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c
@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@
 	int			twl_irq;
 	bool			irq_wake_enabled;
 	atomic_t		wakeirqs;
+	bool			irq_suspend_disabled;
 	struct notifier_block	pm_nb;
 	struct irq_chip		irq_chip;
 	struct irq_domain	*irq_domain;
@@ -137,11 +138,22 @@
 			pdata->irq_wake_enabled = false;
 		}
 
-		disable_irq(pdata->twl_irq);
+		/*
+		 * A wake source must stay enabled: the line is level-triggered, and
+		 * an interrupt arriving while it is disabled masks it until resume,
+		 * so it can no longer wake the system. Once the core suspends the
+		 * interrupts, an armed line wakes the system without running the
+		 * handler, so the suspended I2C bus is not touched.
+		 */
+		pdata->irq_suspend_disabled = !pdata->irq_wake_enabled;
+		if (pdata->irq_suspend_disabled)
+			disable_irq(pdata->twl_irq);
 		break;
 
 	case PM_POST_SUSPEND:
-		enable_irq(pdata->twl_irq);
+		if (pdata->irq_suspend_disabled)
+			enable_irq(pdata->twl_irq);
+		pdata->irq_suspend_disabled = false;
 		break;
 
 	default:
@@ -406,6 +418,10 @@
 	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.name = "twl6030";
 	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.irq_set_type = NULL;
 	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.irq_set_wake = twl6030_irq_set_wake;
+	/* dummy_irq_chip skips irq_set_wake: without this the children's wake
+	 * requests never reach twl6030_irq_set_wake, and the TWL6030 interrupt
+	 * is never armed for wake at suspend */
+	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.flags &= ~IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE;
 
 	twl6030_irq->pm_nb.notifier_call = twl6030_irq_pm_notifier;
 	atomic_set(&twl6030_irq->wakeirqs, 0);
-- 
